<BaseLayout
  title="Aura Homes | Master plan"
  description="The order of the Aura Homes work: the room now, farms, custom stays, water from the air later, and a network that is still a hope."
  descriptor="Master plan"
>
  <main id="top">
    <section class="page-lead">
      <p class="story-kicker">Master plan</p>
      <h1>The order of the work.</h1>
      <p class="story-lede">
        The room is what you can ask for now. The rest is arranged so nothing later pretends to be ready.
      </p>
    </section>
    <div class="page-body">
      <h2>1. The room</h2>
      <p>A finished room on a steel frame, beside the house or on the property. This is the product. See <a href="/rooms">Rooms</a>, and the film on <a href="/">the opening page</a>.</p>
      <h2>2. Aura Farms</h2>
      <p>The same room, with one long side turned into a vertical aeroponic wall. You can ask Aura Homes to build it and place it, or buy it and grow. The page is <a href="/farms">Aura Farms</a>.</p>
      <h2>3. Customs</h2>
      <p>Glass on piles, a deck, and a few rooms for a small resort in Canada or Costa Rica. Drawn for the site. See <a href="/customs">Customs</a>.</p>
      <h2>4. Water, later</h2>
      <p>H20 would set a quiet machine on the roof and a short bottling line inside. It still needs further research. It is not ready to build or to place. The note is on <a href="/water">H20</a>.</p>
      <h2>5. A network we hope for</h2>
      <p>Food and water from these rooms, free to the person who takes them, with an advertiser’s name on the harvest or the jug. That network is not operating. It is described in <a href="/journal/free-food-and-water">the journal</a>, and it is not a signup.</p>
      <h2>6. The tool</h2>
      <p><a href="/build-your-own">Build your own</a> is a walk through the clearing, then three settings: use, glass, and length. Nothing on that page is for sale. The source is on GitHub.</p>
    </div>
  </main>
</BaseLayout>
